{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And he too shall become great, but his younger brother shall be greater than he.</b> He applied to them 'great' and 'small' in the language used of the two luminaries (Genesis 1:16): את המאור הגדול ואת המאור הקטן. And the phrase וזרעו יהיה מלא הגוים — 'and his seed shall become a multitude of nations' — alludes to Joshua, who was destined to come forth from the tribe of Ephraim, for all the nations saw the sign performed through him, as it is said (Joshua 10:12–13): שמש בגבעון דום וירח בעמק אילון, and it is written (ibid.): וידום השמש וירח עמד עד יקום גוי אויביו הלא היא כתובה על ספר הישר. And our Rabbis of blessed memory said: this is the book of Genesis, which is the book of the patriarchs Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, who were called ישרים ('upright ones'). And it is written of him (Joshua 6:27): ויהי ה׳ את יהושע ויהי שמעו בכל הארץ."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:11.739297413Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}